&#8220;But also, Chad Michael Murray invited me,&#8221; she continued of her A Cinderella Story co-star. &#8220;I don&#8217;t want to start any more stuff, but he was like, &#8216;You should come with me,&#8217; and I was like, &#8216;Mm-hmm. Probably I should.&#8217; I mean, what was I, like 16? No, I think I was younger than that &#8212; 15?&#8221;

Duff vs. Lohan was one of the more memorable beefs of the early 2000s, with the two then-teenagers repeatedly sparking reports of a spat over shared romantic woes with Aaron Carter. After the How I Met Your Father star &#8212; whose new album Luck &#8230; or Something dropped last week &#8212; turned up at the Freaky Friday premiere, Lohan famously appeared to seek retribution by crashing Duff&#8217;s Cheaper by the Dozen premiere a few months later.

While on the podcast, Duff told Cooper that she wasn&#8217;t surprised when Lohan gave her a taste of her own medicine. &#8220;I mean, that was, like, my childhood feud, like, nemesis,&#8221; she said. &#8220;I&#8217;m sure my publicist will be like, &#8216;What the f&#8212; are you doing?&#8217; But now it&#8217;s so many years later, like, who cares?

&#8220;Also, Lindsay came up to me at a club once and was like, &#8216;Are we good?'&#8221; Duff added. &#8220;And I was like, &#8216;We&#8217;re good.&#8217; She was like, &#8216;Let&#8217;s take a shot.&#8217; I was like, &#8216;OK!'&#8221;

